+
+### OCR And Document Intelligence
+
+#### [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is one of the strongest open source OCR and document parsing stacks on GitHub. Its README positions it as a toolkit for turning PDFs and images into structured, AI-friendly outputs like JSON and Markdown, with support for multilingual OCR, complex layouts, tables, charts, formulas, and document understanding pipelines. For legal use, this matters because many scanned pleadings, exhibits, and contracts still arrive as image-heavy PDFs. PaddleOCR is not legal-specific, but it is one of the best ingestion layers for legal AI systems. Verified from GitHub: last visible release `2025-11-13`, about `66.5k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `Apache-2.0`.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+- **Stars:** 66.5k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2025-11-13
+- **Category:** ocr, document-parsing, multilingual
+- **Best for:** high-volume OCR and structured extraction from legal PDFs
+
+---
+
+#### [Docling](https://github.com/docling-project/docling)
+> **Description:** Docling is a modern document processing library built for generative AI pipelines. The README emphasizes parsing PDFs, DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, HTML, images, audio, and more into a unified `DoclingDocument` format, with export to Markdown, JSON, and other structured outputs. It also highlights local execution, OCR support, agent integrations, and air-gapped workflows, all of which are relevant to privileged legal data. For firms building private ingestion pipelines, Docling stands out because it combines breadth of formats with strong downstream AI integrations. Verified from GitHub: last commit `2026-03-28`, about `56.6k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `MIT`.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/docling-project/docling](https://github.com/docling-project/docling)
+- **Stars:** 56.6k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03-28
+- **Category:** document-parsing, pdf, ai-ingestion
+- **Best for:** local legal document conversion into Markdown and JSON
+
+---
+
+#### [Marker](https://github.com/datalab-to/marker)
+> **Description:** Marker focuses on converting PDFs to Markdown and JSON quickly and with high accuracy. The project is especially useful when lawyers or legal ops teams need LLM-ready text from contracts, filings, and evidence bundles while preserving structure better than raw OCR. It sits between lightweight PDF text extraction and full document understanding platforms, making it a pragmatic option for search indexing and summarization pipelines. Marker is not a legal tool by itself, but it is a strong open source preprocessing layer for legal AI. Verified from GitHub: updated `2026-01-08`, about `32.3k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `GPL-3.0`.
+
