+#### [olmOCR](https://github.com/allenai/olmocr)
+> **Description:** olmOCR is designed to linearize PDFs and image-based documents into clean, readable text and Markdown. Its README highlights support for equations, tables, handwriting, natural reading order, and header-footer removal, plus tooling for large-scale conversion pipelines. For legal teams, that is useful when scanning archives, discovery productions, or court filings where text quality varies and raw extraction is noisy. It is not the only OCR option here, but it is one of the strongest GitHub repos for LLM-friendly PDF normalization. Verified from GitHub: visible release `2025-10-21`, about `16.6k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `Apache-2.0`.
