+#### [Unstructured](https://github.com/Unstructured-IO/unstructured)
+> **Description:** Unstructured is an open source ETL toolkit for partitioning, cleaning, and chunking more than 25 document types for LLM applications. The README and org overview emphasize transforming complex unstructured data into clean, structured formats and connecting documents to downstream embedding and retrieval systems. For lawyers, this matters because legal knowledge work often starts with messy inputs: PDFs, DOCX files, emails, HTML, and export bundles. Unstructured is widely used because it can serve as the ingestion backbone underneath legal RAG systems without forcing a full application framework. Verified from GitHub: updated `2025-12-30`, about `13.5k` stars, primary language `HTML`, license `Apache-2.0`.
