+#### [Opennyai](https://github.com/OpenNyAI/Opennyai)
+> **Description:** Opennyai is a Python NLP pipeline for Indian legal documents, especially court judgments. The README highlights unified access to three pretrained models: named entity recognition, rhetorical role classification, and extractive summarization. Unlike generic NLP repos, it is focused on judgment text preprocessing and running pretrained legal models on custom inputs, which makes it useful for legal research teams working with case law corpora. It is narrower in scope than a full legal workspace, but it is a genuine legal-tech building block hosted publicly on GitHub. Verified from GitHub: last visible release `2024-05-08`, about `87` stars, primary language `Python`, license `MIT`.
