+#### [pii-redaction](https://github.com/OpenPipe/pii-redaction)
+> **Description:** `pii-redaction` is a smaller but practical Python package for tagging, redacting, or replacing PII in text and JSONL datasets. The README highlights command-line workflows, fake-data replacement, locale-aware substitutions, and a Python API for cleaning datasets before model training or downstream analysis. For legal teams experimenting with internal AI, this kind of lightweight tool can be useful when the goal is to sanitize corpora quickly without deploying a full privacy platform. It is not as broad as Presidio, but it is a clear and focused GitHub repository. Verified from GitHub: public repo active in early `2026`, about `87` stars, primary language `Python`, license `MIT`.
