+### OCR And Document Intelligence
+
+#### [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is one of the strongest open source OCR and document parsing stacks on GitHub. Its README positions it as a toolkit for turning PDFs and images into structured, AI-friendly outputs like JSON and Markdown, with support for multilingual OCR, complex layouts, tables, charts, formulas, and document understanding pipelines. For legal use, this matters because many scanned pleadings, exhibits, and contracts still arrive as image-heavy PDFs. PaddleOCR is not legal-specific, but it is one of the best ingestion layers for legal AI systems. Verified from GitHub: last visible release `2025-11-13`, about `66.5k` stars, primary language `Python`, license `Apache-2.0`.
